>>
endobj
186 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (The main threats to this industry are the high raw material costs resulting from the shortage in milk supply \(Tibballs n.d.\). This increase in the price of inputs is passed to the consumer which already has lower levels of disposable income leading to a decline in revenue for the ice cream industry \(Beckers et al. 2024\). Furthermore, since local production has become more expensive, the level of international competition has risen intensifying the price competition and potentially eroding profits \(Francis 2024\). )
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
187 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (With the rising level of health-conscious consumers occurring, a key opportunity within this market is maximising on these health and wellness trends. This can be achieved by reducing sugar and fat content within ice cream, in addition to adding ingredients with nutritional benefits. This encourages the adoption of ice cream to a wider demographic that includes individuals who have dietary requirements or are trying to lose weight. Capitalising on this trend is pivotal in remaining competitive within the industry.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
